WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.167
I'm gonna give the team.

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.919
You tell me the inconvenient
truth about this playoff team

00:00:02.919 --> 00:00:05.046
and what can hold them back.
- Gotcha.

00:00:05.046 --> 00:00:06.673
- The New Orleans Saints.
- The New Orleans Saints.

00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:08.341
I'll tell you one of
the inconvenient truths there.

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:09.801
- What's the excuse
they've been leaning on?

00:00:09.801 --> 00:00:11.094
- Well, I will say this.

00:00:11.094 --> 00:00:12.721
I think one of
the inconvenient truths

00:00:12.721 --> 00:00:14.514
and it's been exposed
a little bit

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:17.142
is Drew Brees and what he can
bring to the Saints offense.

00:00:17.142 --> 00:00:19.185
I know. We're gonna
open up a can of worms here.

00:00:19.185 --> 00:00:21.146
- What do you want? What do
you want, Who Dat Nation?

00:00:21.146 --> 00:00:22.856
- But we talk about offenses
all the time, right?
- Yes!

00:00:22.856 --> 00:00:25.066
- How great offenses
make you defend the whole field.
- Sure.

00:00:25.066 --> 00:00:28.778
- But he's not— at this age,
39 years old, he's not capable

00:00:28.778 --> 00:00:31.448
of scrambling out of the pocket,
making plays that way.

00:00:31.448 --> 00:00:33.742
- Monday against Carolina,
when the rush got there

00:00:33.742 --> 00:00:35.410
the play was over.
- Exactly right.

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:38.371
He's not gonna make
any physically demanding plays

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:40.582
that we're gonna go,
"Whoa, there was nobody open

00:00:40.582 --> 00:00:42.167
the protection
wasn't that great

00:00:42.167 --> 00:00:43.918
and he still made it happen."

00:00:43.918 --> 00:00:47.881
And, hey, listen. He throws
the ball shorter downfield.

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:49.507
He's tied with Eli Manning

00:00:49.507 --> 00:00:51.301
for 28th in football
in yards in the air.

00:00:51.301 --> 00:00:53.636
- Intended air yards—
him and Eli tied.

00:00:53.636 --> 00:00:56.389
- Yes, so, again, they can win the Super Bowl with him.
- Yes.

00:00:56.389 --> 00:00:59.517
- But there is little issues
with his game

00:00:59.517 --> 00:01:01.853
and when you see teams
take away their screens

00:01:01.853 --> 00:01:03.438
and things like that

00:01:03.438 --> 00:01:05.690
that offense doesn't work
as smoothly because nobody's

00:01:05.690 --> 00:01:07.984
scared of Drew Brees
throwing bombs over their head.

00:01:07.984 --> 00:01:10.862
- There's one team that everybody
is piling on right now—
- Yeah.

00:01:10.862 --> 00:01:13.156
- Cuz they're excited
they no longer have a bye.
- Right.

00:01:13.156 --> 00:01:14.699
- The Patriots.
- Ooh.

00:01:14.699 --> 00:01:16.284
- I'm still scared
of the Patriots.

00:01:16.284 --> 00:01:18.078
- Yes, you should be.
- Just gonna put that out there.

00:01:18.078 --> 00:01:19.579
But what is their
inconvenient truth?

00:01:19.579 --> 00:01:22.582
- Their inconvenient truth
is that Gronk

00:01:22.582 --> 00:01:25.126
is no longer the greatest
mismatch in football.

00:01:25.126 --> 00:01:26.503
That has ended.
- Wow.

00:01:26.503 --> 00:01:29.130
- Gronk is no longer
holding the trophy

00:01:29.130 --> 00:01:30.924
as the best tight end
in the game.

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:32.801
And I would even argue
that he's not

00:01:32.801 --> 00:01:35.136
even Brady's go-to guy
all the time.

00:01:35.136 --> 00:01:37.847
I think there's been big moments
during the year where he's gone

00:01:37.847 --> 00:01:39.390
"I'm gonna go
to Josh Gordon here.

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:41.101
I trust him in this situation."

00:01:41.101 --> 00:01:43.269
And since Josh Gordon's
been there, he's been targeted

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:45.063
more than any other receiver
on their team.

00:01:45.063 --> 00:01:48.108
- I want a real truth.
- But yes, Gronk has lost a step.

00:01:48.108 --> 00:01:50.777
I do think he's lost his
intensity, and I

00:01:50.777 --> 00:01:52.904
don't think— hey, there's a reason
New England was rumored

00:01:52.904 --> 00:01:55.031
to be trying to trade him
in the offseason.

00:01:55.031 --> 00:01:57.033
I think they saw a few,
you know

00:01:57.033 --> 00:02:00.703
dents in the armor here
that were about to come about.

00:02:00.703 --> 00:02:02.247
- A few more dents in the armor.
- Yeah.

00:02:02.247 --> 00:02:05.250
- L.A. Rams. This offense
has been struggling.
- Yeah.

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:07.127
- What's the inconvenient truth
about the Rams?

00:02:07.127 --> 00:02:09.003
- People are gonna point
to Jared Goff, right?

00:02:09.003 --> 00:02:10.713
- They are.
- Who's been in Strugglesville.

00:02:10.713 --> 00:02:12.132
I mean, yes.
- One touchdown
the last three weeks.

00:02:12.132 --> 00:02:13.675
- It's not been perfect.
OK, I get that.

00:02:13.675 --> 00:02:14.968
So he deserves
some of the blame

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:16.678
but the real inconvenient truth

00:02:16.678 --> 00:02:18.638
is the interior part
of their offensive line.
- Really?

00:02:18.638 --> 00:02:21.224
- They got big-time issues
there, and that's really

00:02:21.224 --> 00:02:23.977
the biggest reason you've seen
all three of their losses.

00:02:23.977 --> 00:02:27.063
Sheldon Rankins whupped them
for the Saints, OK?

00:02:27.063 --> 00:02:28.481
Eddie Goldman and Akiem Hicks

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:30.024
whupped them when the
Bears beat them, right?

00:02:30.024 --> 00:02:31.651
- Dominated.
- Fletcher Cox and your Eagles

00:02:31.651 --> 00:02:33.486
whupped their butt
this past week.

00:02:33.486 --> 00:02:35.321
- I don't know how that happened.
- That's the inconvenient truth.

00:02:35.321 --> 00:02:37.490
Now they can't win any of those
battles on the inside.

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:39.492
Their running game's
not working, and, of course

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:41.161
pressure is getting
into Goff's face

00:02:41.161 --> 00:02:42.495
and he's not as sharp, either.

00:02:42.495 --> 00:02:44.581
- I have one more inconvenient truth
- One more—

00:02:44.581 --> 00:02:46.833
- And it's me to you.
- Oh, gosh.

00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:49.711
It's inconvenient that I gotta
work with you on a daily basis.

00:02:49.711 --> 00:02:52.380
- All right, well, now I'm not
afraid to say it anymore.

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:55.592
I can't believe I'm saying this.
- What?
- He's over my shoulder.

00:02:55.592 --> 00:02:57.760
I don't think Aaron Rodgers
is the best quarterback

00:02:57.760 --> 00:02:59.262
in the NFL anymore.

00:02:59.262 --> 00:03:01.598
- You sound like my son Phillip,
who last week

00:03:01.598 --> 00:03:04.058
was watching Patrick Mahomes
on Thursday night and said

00:03:04.058 --> 00:03:06.603
"Mahomes is better than
Aaron Rodgers now, Dad."

00:03:06.603 --> 00:03:09.397
- Look, I'm just happy
that one Simms in the family

00:03:09.397 --> 00:03:11.608
has some sense,
but I think that Patrick Mahomes

00:03:11.608 --> 00:03:13.651
is far and away better
than Aaron Rodgers.

00:03:13.651 --> 00:03:15.820
- Get out of the studio.
Get out of the studio.

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:17.447
- We have a shrine.
- This is blasphemy!

00:03:17.447 --> 00:03:19.699
- I think he is.
- He's the second shrine in here.

00:03:19.699 --> 00:03:20.992
Blasphemy. Get out.
I don't even know who you are.

00:03:20.992 --> 00:03:22.994
- I think that that should
become the primary shrine.

00:03:22.994 --> 00:03:24.996
- Where is Adam Lefkoe? Who—
what—where did my host go?

00:03:25.038 --> 00:03:27.665
- I'm just saying that—
- He doesn't have Tyreek Hill

00:03:27.665 --> 00:03:30.210
he didn't have Kareem Hunt,
he doesn't have Andy Reid

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:33.713
he doesn't have Sammy Watkins,
he doesn't have Travis Kelce.

00:03:33.713 --> 00:03:36.466
♪ Aaron Rodgers,
you're still the greatest ♪

00:03:36.466 --> 00:03:39.510
♪ But even the greatest
needs help sometimes ♪

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:42.430
- I just— I'm not saying
he's worse than two.

00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:44.766
- Yeah.
- I'm just sayin' he's not one.

00:03:44.766 --> 00:03:46.976
- It's the first year—
I'm not gonna lie

00:03:46.976 --> 00:03:48.561
I've had moments where I've—
- Say it. Say it.

00:03:48.561 --> 00:03:50.230
- Nope. I've had moments
where I've gone

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:52.232
"Huh, this is getting
kinda close."

00:03:52.232 --> 00:03:53.942
- You said, "Huh."
- I said, "Huh.

00:03:53.942 --> 00:03:55.443
This is getting kinda close."
- Wow.

00:03:55.443 --> 00:03:56.861
- But I'm still not gonna
give him the nod yet.

00:03:56.861 --> 00:03:58.696
- The best part
that it was Phillip

00:03:58.696 --> 00:04:00.698
is I can keep "Simms &amp; Lefkoe"
and just replace you with him.

00:04:00.698 --> 00:04:02.367
- Oh, thanks.
- I love that.

00:04:02.367 --> 00:04:04.244
- Thanks a lot.
- Me and an eight-year-old

00:04:04.244 --> 00:04:06.621
comin' next week.

